as defining my  life is non-human  talking about me as if I was not there  and my father turns to him and said I I  really hope you do not speak to other  patients in this way and the searches  just looked at him and my dad said I'm a  medical doctor as well and this is in no  way the way that we were taught to speak  to people Francesco's injury left him  paralyzed from the neck down with years  of physical therapy his progress would  defy odds but four years after the  accident he struggled with depression  tell us about your recovery everyday  adapting to what it means to have a new  life redefining herself so I could not  look in a mirror for being be in a room  with a lot of windows because all I  would notice was wheelchair you didn't  want to see yourself in a chair I could  not because all I would notice was these  four wheels that I sat on and not the  person that was in it and I would burst  into tears every time that I saw it at  what point did you say I've got to do  something this has got to change the day  that everything changed for me was  hearing Barbara Walters  announced on TV that Christopher Reeve  passed away he was the biggest advocate  for people with spinal cord injuries and  so the day that he passed I realized  that my Superman had disappeared and  then I also realized that I had not done  enough to take responsibility for what  happened in my life so when you finally  looked at yourself in the mirror you  thought I got to do what I did not look  like myself my skin looked like it was  10 years older than it was it was very  dry anything and everything that could  go wrong with your skin went wrong with  my skin because it stopped sweating  because of my injury with help from his  father a medical doctor also trained in  homeopathy Francesco would create his  own skin care blend at home and when  they started to notice that my skin  started to look good my sister said well  if it looks good on Francesco I'm just  gonna steal a couple of these vials and  just use them and then my mom started to  say you know I'm gonna steal a couple of  vials as well so I created this triangle  of kleptomaniacs  of these products that we were making in  the kitchen but it was just something  that I was doing for myself humble  beginnings for what would become  skincare brand Clarke's botanicals it's  more than a company it represents a  renewed sense of purpose for Francesco  so after Clarke's botanical started I  emailed the CEO of the Christopher Reeve  Foundation and then I met with every  director I was just meeting with them  because I wanted to do more and to be  involved and I felt like it was a very  grassroots way of me giving back to  something that gave me a reason for  living about five weeks they called me  and they asked me to become one of their  national ambassadors and a lot to you it  meant the world to me one of your  mantras is vanity saved my life I like  the juxtaposition of the phrase vanity  saved my life because it catches you  off-guard  and it makes you think that's such a  stupid thing to say  with beauty there's a sense of  vulnerability it means a lot to me to  connect to other people on that in that  way I am so smitten with him Norah you  know we did something on him in the  magazine that's how I met him and then I  met him in person at the magazine and  was listening to his story said this is  a good story can I tell this story but  the thing about him is that he is so  determined and so resilient and I think  outside of the fashion industry you  might not have heard of Clarke's  botanicals but a lot of people have  heard of it that's why my skin looks so  radiant today John as you were  commenting yes right and so the company  is now a ten million dollar business and  he has already defied the odds he does  believe that he will work again  he will walk again rather he's already  moving arms and legs that they said  would never happen and he believes that  somewhere in the future that 